Chad.text_english:
Article 296. - 
Anyone who, with intent to destroy in whole or in part a national, ethnic, racial, or religious group, or a group defined by any other arbitrary criterion, commits against members of that group any of the following acts is guilty of genocide and shall be punished by imprisonment for life:

a) assassination;

b) murder;

e) causing serious bodily or mental harm;

d) deliberately inflicting on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical destruction, in whole or in part;

