Timor-Leste.text_english:
Article 123
Genocide
1. Whoever, with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, ethnic, racial or religious group, commits:
a) Murder or serious bodily or psychological harm to members of the group;

b) Acts that by any means prevent the procreation or birth of members of the group;

c) Rape, sexual slavery, forced prostitution, forced pregnancy, forced sterilization or any other form of sexual violence of comparable gravity;

d) Separation by violent means of members of the group to another group;

e) Acts that by violent means prevent the group from settling or remaining in a geographical area that is traditionally or historically recognized as belonging to it;

f) Subjection of the group to cruel, degrading or inhuman conditions of life or treatment, likely to bring about its total or partial destruction;

g) Widespread confiscation or seizure of property belonging to members of the group;

h) Prohibition of certain commercial, industrial, or professional activities for members of the group;

i) Spread of an epidemic likely to cause death or harm to members of the group;

j) Prohibition, omission, or impediment by any means of providing adequate humanitarian assistance to members of the group to combat epidemics or serious food shortages;

is punishable by a prison sentence of 15 to 30 years.

2. Anyone who publicly and directly incites the practice of genocide is punishable by a prison sentence of 5 to 15 years.

